Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.36 phase 3: hold the win jingle for 4 s of music time while turbo keeps the music at 1x

Design: docs/P6.36_TURBO_MUSIC.md, owner decision 2026-10-29. The win jingle
(SOUND_WIN_JINGLE, a looping SEP track that never ends by itself) is cut about
a second after the knock-out at turbo, when the field's music call that
follows the battle arrives. With Turbo music on 1x and fast-forward running,
playing the jingle starts a hold (dw3_port_audio_music_request,
port/audio/turbo_music.c). The one music call of `FIELDSTG_updateField`
(`field_mode/field.c`, the area's music or "none") asks
`dw3_port_audio_field_music`: during the hold it is kept back (the latest one
wins) and `updateSoundLoading` (`sound.c`), once per frame, plays or stops it
after 4 s of music time (240 music ticks, 200 on EU-PAL). Any other music
call ends the hold at once and goes through: an exclusive `playSound` (a
battle's own track, an event's), a `stopSound` of the jingle, `stopAllSounds`
(a new battle, a movie, the title, a restart); a request kept back is then
dropped. The game does not wait: only the field's call is deferred. With Turbo
music on Fast or turbo off no hold starts and every hook is a no-op: the
original calls. Replay scenarios `us/eu-turbo-music-hold`, `-nohold`,
`-hold-stopped`.

